  "note": "Judgement identity as DATA, replayed through the implementation. `receipt_core_digest` answers 'which bytes'; `judgement_digest` answers 'which judgement', and they stopped being the same question once two contracts could judge one core. The first version of this file recomputed both digests from a stored core and compared them with stored values -- which a mutation showed proved nothing about the projector. Each case now ships the exact snapshot bytes, receipt bytes and CAS, and the harness projects them and compares the identities the graph actually carries.",
